## 3. Target Audience & Searcher Profile

The primary searcher is a renter or potential mover who has been priced out of a California coastal market or is relocating to California from out of state and is in the **discovery or early comparison stage** of the rental journey. They may be a remote worker with location flexibility, a young adult leaving a family home, a working-class family seeking more space per dollar, or a retiree on fixed income. Their specific problem is that they know California has a reputation for high housing costs and they want to know which cities or regions are exceptions before they invest time in a deeper search. They expect a scannable list with real numbers (rent ranges, home price ranges) rather than vague affordability language, organized by city or region.

